            <ArticleTitle>Nursing care: use of digital learning objects with chronic illnesses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This poster focuses on two digital learning objects which use hypertext, animations and video. The digital learning objects for Obesity and Dyslipidemia are being evaluated through a research project implemented by the undergraduate nursing students at The Federal University do Rio Grande do Sul (UFRGS). The project &quot;Digital Learning Objects: Obesity and Dyslipidemia&quot; is designed to subsidize the questions about non-communicable chronic diseases in the academic and professional routine in primary health care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
